          "certainty_level": "widely_supported"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "s7_C06",
      "text": "On that side of the ledger: mass-driven and environment-driven quenching stay separable out to z~1, star formation has ceased in 30%-70% of satellites, and satellite quenching is reported as dominant for satellites below 10^10 solar masses, with a delayed-then-rapid history — a 2-4 Gyr delay, then an e-folding time under 0.8 Gyr.",
      "bound_entry_ids": [
        "clc_agn_010_halo_environment_satellite_axis"
      ],
      "max_allowed_tier": "commonly_probably",
