    },
    {
      "sentence_id": "s7_D02",
      "text": "Gas retention and low star-formation efficiency can qualify simple gas-removal accounts: SFR-matched AGN hosts show no molecular-gas difference, some z~0.7 quenched galaxies retain large molecular reservoirs, and some massive quiescent disks retain substantial atomic hydrogen.",
